WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.970
<b>Sea Charts and Fishmen</b>

38
00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.600
This looks suspiciously like a

39
00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:02.980
treasure map. And it seems to be
pointing to Cocoyashi Village.

40
00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.650
I can't believe you have the nerve
to go through my personal belongings!

41
00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.610
That's my map and it has
nothing to do with you!

42
00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:16.200
So angry... Is there
something on your mind?

43
00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.330
What is this?!

44
00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.420
Why are all these guys dead?
What happened?

45
00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.960
The pirate hunter Zoro did it!

46
00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.760
Why weren't you here, Hatchi? Huh?

47
00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.670
This could've been prevented,
had you been here!

48
00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.870
Of course it could've!

49
00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.890
Had I only been here!

50
00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.520
It's unforgivable!

51
00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:42.010
We get it. You weren't here.

52
00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.140
So you don't know where
he is, is that right?

53
00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:48.270
Well, let me think about it...

54
00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.690
I saw one guy. Yeah, that's right...

55
00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.610
He was a slightly
suspicious swordsman type.

56
00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.410
That's him!

57
00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.740
You did see him, you idiot!

58
00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.370
So where did he go?!

59
00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:08.880
He told me he wanted to see Arlong,
so I gave him a ride to Cocoyashi Village.

60
00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:14.920
Excellent... That means we
don't have any need to hurry.

61
00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.260
He's going to come straight to me.

62
00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.140
Sorry, Arlong, but if I had known
you were going to be back so soon,

63
00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.560
I would have kept him here for you.

64
00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.020
But he said he was a guest and
I thought I should get him

65
00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.520
to the village as fast as I could.

66
00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.190
Zoro, huh?

67
00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:33.690
Which means if I can buy
just a little more time...

68
00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.650
Why do you keep
getting in the way?!

69
00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:45.910
Everything's so close to
working out! So close!

70
00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.050
Damn you, Nami!
You want a fight, don't ya?

71
00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.510
This is your fault, Usopp.

72
00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:04.520
You're the one getting in the way.

73
00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.930
This is what you get
for messing with Arlong.

74
00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.810
Nami, you've
really disappointed me.

75
00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.470
Even after you stole
our ship and ran off,

76
00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.560
Luffy had complete faith in you.
He trusts you completely,

77
00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.730
and you haven't even
shown an ounce of guilt!

78
00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.030
How can you betray someone like that?!

79
00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.910
Are you really that cold-hearted?

80
00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.080
The only thing I trust is money.

81
00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:27.420
Those dumb enough to
be fooled deserve it.

82
00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:28.790
How can you say that?!

83
00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:34.210
You idiots... It was
going according to plan.

84
00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:41.700
I'm not about to let you and your
friends ruin eight long years of hard work.

85
00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.060
So long, Usopp. It's just business.

86
00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.350
You understand.

87
00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.640
Heh. Well, I'll be damned.

88
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.440
Looks like you became a
pirate while you were gone.

89
00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.190
So long...?

90
00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.550
What, like you're gonna kill me?!

91
00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:03.570
That's right... I wouldn't
underestimate me.

92
00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.120
Aww, crap...

93
00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.870
If I stay here, I'm a dead man.

94
00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.160
Special attack...!

95
00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:15.630
...Smoke Star!

96
00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.300
Now's my chance!

97
00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:29.760
This is just like
something you'd think up.

98
00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:30.810
Nami!

99
00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.270
Don't do this...

100
00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.240
It's for my business.

101
00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.750
This was my only choice.

102
00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.710
Nami, how could you...?

103
00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.250
Now go and die.

104
00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:16.480
I can't believe it! Big
Sis Nami... killed Big Bro Usopp!

105
00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.810
Your wish came true... You died at sea.

106
00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.380
Nami.
I'm sorry for doubting you.

107
00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.910
Without question... You're our friend.

108
00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.410
Friend, huh?

109
00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.670
There's only one reason
I joined this group.

110
00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.570
And that's to buy Cocoyashi
Village from you!

111
00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:40.460
Ya got that? Just business. Not friends.

112
00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:45.470
Keep your end of the deal and
I'll have those berries soon.

113
00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.470
Yes, of course!

114
00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:51.770
I'd rather cut my stomach open and die
than break a promise concerning money.

115
00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:54.140
That's the kind of man I am.

116
00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.940
Glad to hear it, Arlong.
You know the score.

117
00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:01.940
She gives me the creeps.

118
00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.740
Oh, what a great
woman she's become!

119
00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:11.950
He's dead... She killed him!

120
00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.750
That witch killed him!

121
00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:19.750
There it is! Arlong Park!

122
00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:26.260
Hey! Keep up the pace, cow!

123
00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.760
I feel sorry for it.

124
00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.430
Sanji's kicks must've
really taken their toll!

125
00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.020
Not that way!
Go to your other left!

126
00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.020
To the building stupid!

127
00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.850
It's almost like we're flying!

128
00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:00.950
Almost?!

129
00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:03.000
We are flying, you moron!

130
00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.920
No! We're falling!

131
00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.060
Hm?

132
00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.440
Landing successful!

133
00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.340
Huh?

134
00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:23.400
Hey! Zoro!

135
00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:37.370
Awesome. We're here, guys!

136
00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.420
What the hell...?

137
00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:43.040
are you doing?!

138
00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:47.400
Whaddya mean? We're here
to pick up Nami. Duh.

139
00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.430
How come you haven't found her yet?

140
00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.430
Oh, yeah. And what about
Usopp and Johnny?

141
00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.140
Usopp! Oh, no!

142
00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:57.430
C'mon, we gotta hurry!

143
00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:58.930
Why, what's wrong?!

144
00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.100
That dumbass has
been caught by Arlong!

145
00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.150
We gotta hurry before they kill him!

146
00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.940
He's already dead!

147
00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.780
What?!

148
00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.780
We're too late!

149
00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:13.570
Big Bro Usopp is dead!

150
00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.740
Nami... murdered him!

151
00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:25.000
<b>West Coast,
Cocoyashi Village</b>

152
00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:23.250
– C'mon! Hurry up!
– What's the deal?!

153
00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:25.420
The Marines are here! We're saved!

154
00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:28.170
Some survivors from Gosa managed
to contact the government

155
00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.970
and they told 'em what happened!

156
00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:33.440
Now the Marines
are here to rescue us all!

157
00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:34.430
See?!

158
00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.660
Finally! It's over!

159
00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:42.020
Now we get to leave
this horrible place!

160
00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:48.440
So this is
the infamous Arlong Park!

161
00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:53.320
What is the world coming to when pirate
scum can set up such an opulent base?!

162
00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:54.910
Listen up, men!

163
00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:57.480
Our noble mission today
is one of extraction!

164
00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.000
We must rescue the survivors
of the town of Gosa,

165
00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.420
which was savagely destroyed
by the Arlong Pirates!

166
00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.660
But I am left to wonder...

167
00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.170
Would our brand of
swift and terrible justice

168
00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:14.380
allow us to simply overlook the decadent
fortress of these unchecked brutes?!

169
00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.080
Sir, no, sir!

170
00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:22.570
Correct! Our unit must annihilate
Arlong and his men! Prepare for battle at once!

171
00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:23.900
Yes, sir!

172
00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:26.570
Is that right? Marine branch 77?

173
00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:28.360
That's right. That's what I said.

174
00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:29.570
A newcomer.

175
00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.570
We'll have someone negotiate
with the man in charge.

176
00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:34.570
If two million isn't enough
to keep them from

177
00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.910
trying anything funny, then kill
every last one of them.

178
00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.860
Oh, no!
The Marines have opened fire!

179
00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.170
Arlong! Watch out!

180
00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.100
Whoa. He crushed a cannonball.

181
00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.060
Those jaws are terrifying!

182
00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.560
So what now? Are the talks...?

183
00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.390
Canceled.

184
00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.900
Alright! Let's do it!

185
00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.770
I've
been waitin' for a good fight!

186
00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.530
It's gonna be a bloodbath!

187
00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.360
Choo. Hold on, guys, not so fast.

188
00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:21.660
<b>Officer Chew
(Kisser Fishman)
Arlong Pirates</b>

189
00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:21.200
There's no need to expend so much energy
just to take out the trash. Choo.

190
00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.910
Just leave it to us!

191
00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:28.540
<b>Officer Kuroobi
(Ray Fishman)
Arlong Pirates</b>

192
00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:26.960
What foolish humans they are
to pick a fight with us.

193
00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:28.540
In our own waters, too.

194
00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:32.120
Those Marines don't stand a chance
against three of our leaders.

195
00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.220
I doubt that ship will make it

196
00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:36.130
a full three minutes!

197
00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.350
That's odd.

198
00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:41.880
Commodore.
Seems that cannonball was a dud.

199
00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.010
Fire another!

200
00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.020
This is a signal of open hostility!

201
00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.560
Never drop your guard when
you're dealing with fishmen!

202
00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:48.310
Sir!

203
00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:52.760
Man down!

204
00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.820
It's one of them! Attack!

205
00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:56.530
Stand down, right now!

206
00:11:57.870 --> 00:11:59.600
One of Arlong's men, yes?

207
00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:04.160
I am Commodore Purinpurin
of Marines branch number 77.

208
00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.620
Allow me to elaborate.

209
00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:09.500
You see, we are a somewhat
well-known elite Marine unit.

210
00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.880
Do you understand
what I'm telling you, fishman?

211
00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.630
If you wish to live,
surrender immediately and...

212
00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:15.740
Commodore!

213
00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:18.090
– What have you done to him?!
– You killed him!

214
00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:20.680
What's all this shaking?!

215
00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:23.510
Don't tell me there are
fishmen under the ship!

216
00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:30.270
I really am sorry to
inconvenience you like this,

217
00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.940
but we just took the liberty
of removing your rudder.

218
00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.690
Is that okay?

219
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.400
– Uh! You what?
– Commodore!

220
00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:41.120
Choo. Don't worry, I didn't
hit any of his vital organs.

221
00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.910
Commodore, I have a question.

222
00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:45.860
It's just hypothetical, of course.

223
00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:49.620
If one were to move a large reef
directly into a strong current,

224
00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:52.100
what do you suppose
would happen to the ocean?

225
00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.090
What?!

226
00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.540
No. Moving a whole reef?

227
00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:02.540
That can't be done,
it's just not possible!

228
00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.300
Put it down over there, Hachi.

229
00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.140
Right!

230
00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.640
Uh...! Commodore!

231
00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.600
A giant
whirlpool has just appeared!

232
00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.940
The rudder isn't working!

233
00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:11.690
What?!

234
00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.690
I told you.
We removed the rudder.

235
00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:21.660
So now this rudderless ship is headed
straight... choo... to the sea floor.

236
00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.050
They're dead.

237
00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:43.760
That's right. And so is hope.

238
00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.100
Time to face the truth.

239
00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.270
There's no way to escape
Arlong's control.

240
00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.230
I'll bet you're tired.

241
00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:56.400
No, I didn't even break a sweat.

242
00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.900
We know everything about these waters,

243
00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.360
from the winds to the depths.
It was quite easy.

244
00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.950
With our expert knowledge of these
waters, no one can beat us.

245
00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.910
True, but let's not
forget Nami's charts.

246
00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.500
Indeed. They are excellent charts.

247
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:12.950
If we could persuade Nami to do
this for all the world's oceans,

248
00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.090
we would be the undisputed
rulers of the sea forever.

249
00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.340
I know. Nami's brilliant.

250
00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.290
In fact, she could be
critical in the creation

251
00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.760
of the Arlong Empire.
It's just a shame!

252
00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:24.840
A shame?

253
00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:27.630
He promised to let Nami
and Cocoyashi Village go

254
00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:30.140
once she saves up 100 million berries.

255
00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.970
Oh, no! Seriously?!

256
00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.020
Whatever you do,
you can't let her leave!

257
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:34.820
You can't!

258
00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.020
I have to!

259
00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.360
That was what we
agreed upon eight years ago!

260
00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:44.450
I'm the kind of man who always keeps
my promises when it comes to money.

261
00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:46.200
Always.

262
00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.720
Say another word and you'll regret it!

263
00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.060
Easy, Luffy.

264
00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.730
This has nothing to do with Johnny.

265
00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:53.960
Go on, believe whatever you want.

266
00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.630
But I know what I saw!
Nami killed Big Bro Usopp!

267
00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:01.840
Shut your mouth! Never in a
million years would Nami kill Usopp!

268
00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:03.590
She wouldn't do that to her friends!

269
00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:05.680
But... But I saw it!

270
00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.620
What was that about friends, Luffy?

271
00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:12.490
– Nami!
– What are you doing here?

272
00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.140
What are we doing here?

273
00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:17.090
You're our friend! We came to get you.

274
00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:19.680
– What a pest.
– Nami?

275
00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.120
Friends, huh? Don't make me laugh.

276
00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.860
You're just pathetic enough
to deserve each other.

277
00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.360
Damn you!

278
00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.830
You killed him! I watched you do it!

279
00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.830
And now... Big Bro Usopp is gone!

280
00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.510
Yep, that's right.

281
00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:36.790
So why don't you kill me
and get your revenge?

282
00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.960
Eh... What?

283
00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:40.990
Word to the wise, fellas.

284
00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:43.490
Because of your "friend's" stupidity,

285
00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:47.760
Arlong is preparing to kill Zoro
along with his entire crew.

286
00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:51.500
And I don't care how monstrously
strong you guys think you are,

287
00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:54.140
you're no match for the real monsters.

288
00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.520
Hi, Nami! It's me, Sanji!

289
00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:01.360
Let's run away together!

290
00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:04.650
Can it, Romeo! This isn't
the time or place for that!

291
00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:05.850
Excuse me.

292
00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.550
Love is like a hurricane, so back off.

293
00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.470
Hey, look at me
when I'm talking to you!

294
00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.490
Nami, where is Usopp?

295
00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:15.290
– With the fishes.
– Damn it! Cut the crap!

296
00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:21.340
How sad,
a swordsman striking a lady.

297
00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:23.960
Idiot! Can't you see
what's happening here?

298
00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.590
You're starting to piss me off.

299
00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:29.840
Heh. If someone had stopped me
that easily, I'd be mad, too.

300
00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.390
What?

301
00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.890
You... should watch your mouth.

302
00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:37.140
I'll say whatever I want, bastard.

303
00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:38.440
Big Bros!

304
00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:39.980
We're all in this together, okay?

305
00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:41.650
This is no time to fight!

306
00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:42.730
Your pal's right.

307
00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:45.120
Now quit your bickering
and leave while you still can.

308
00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:48.950
You outsiders have no right
to butt into this island's affairs.

309
00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.600
Don't you get it yet?

310
00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.770
The only reason
I got close to you idiots

311
00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:55.370
was so that I could rob you
of everything you had.

312
00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:58.080
But now that you're broke,
it looks like the dream's dead.

313
00:16:58.090 --> 00:16:59.580
So go, take your ship.

314
00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:04.420
Go on. Find a navigator dumb enough
to join you and go to the Grand Line.

315
00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.710
Continue on your quest to find
the One Piece or whatever.

316
00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:09.930
Just leave here! You're an eyesore!

317
00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:14.810
Goodbye now.

318
00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.470
Nami...

319
00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.730
Big Bro Luffy!

320
00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.150
– Sleepy.
– Sleep?!

321
00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.380
At a time like this?!

322
00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:29.740
In the middle of the road?!

323
00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.030
Well, I'm pretty tired.

324
00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:34.450
I'm not gonna butt into their affairs.

325
00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.160
I'm not interested.

326
00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:38.620
But I'm not leaving either.

327
00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:39.580
– Night.
– Huh?!

328
00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:47.460
Fine.

329
00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.550
Whatever! Just go ahead and die!

330
00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.680
Hey! Big Bro Zoro!

331
00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.060
What on earth are you thinking?! C'mon!

332
00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:02.810
Did you forget that
Arlong is out to kill us?

333
00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.560
We should be running away!

334
00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:08.310
Now that we know what Nami's really like,
there isn't a single good reason why

335
00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:09.740
we should stay on this island.

336
00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:15.060
Right. Understood. You're not leaving.

337
00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:17.560
Sorry to cut our reunion short,
but I won't stay.

338
00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:19.040
My role as guide ends here.

339
00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.450
Yeah, I'm with him.

340
00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.370
I don't want to deliberately
get myself killed.

341
00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.750
Fine. I'll see ya around.

342
00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:28.250
Until we meet again, Big Bro!

343
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.970
Take care, you guys!

344
00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:31.420
You, too!

345
00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:51.440
Hey, do you still honestly believe
that Nami could've killed Usopp?

346
00:18:57.870 --> 00:18:59.830
When she did that...

347
00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.500
It's for my business.

348
00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:06.960
This was my only choice.

349
00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:15.760
When she did that... Nami stabbed her
own hand to make it look like she stabbed me!

350
00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.100
I can't believe she did that for me!

351
00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:24.310
But it's a good thing she did, otherwise
I'd be fish food right now for sure!

352
00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.480
But what do I do?!

353
00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:30.110
A manly man like me can't just turn
tail and run after being saved!

354
00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:31.480
One step at a time!

355
00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.570
Right now I gotta hurry and find Zoro!

356
00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.320
Is that him up ahead?

357
00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:38.810
It is! It's Zoro!

358
00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:41.850
So Nami didn't kill him.
Is that what you're saying?

359
00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.490
Am I wrong?

360
00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:44.950
Huh. Well, who knows?

361
00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.500
I always thought of her as
kind of a small-time crook

362
00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:50.170
who wouldn't even watch
a guy die, let alone kill him.

363
00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:51.630
But maybe she just snapped.

364
00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.550
Wait. What'd you say?

365
00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.920
She's not small-time!

366
00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:58.220
Is she all you think about?!

367
00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.100
He's alive.

368
00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:05.470
Well, he was.

369
00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:08.560
I hope he still is.

370
00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:29.040
Jeez, Nami. You sure know
how to trash a place.

371
00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:32.090
Hey. What's wrong?

372
00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:36.090
Nothing. I'm just
resting a little, that's all.

373
00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.880
You mean to tell me that
poring over a treasure map

374
00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:43.310
after wrecking a house
is how you relax?

375
00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.130
You're not fooling me.

376
00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:47.270
Now fess up already.
What's bothering you?

377
00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:53.320
It's okay. You can
tell me anything, remember?

378
00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:56.900
Something happened
to make me mad. It's nothing.

379
00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:59.780
Those guys? Who are they?

380
00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.320
You know?

381
00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.990
Yeah. I met some captain guy.

382
00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:06.580
He seemed kind of liar-ish, though.

383
00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.840
Now I see.

384
00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:18.300
Yeah, that would hit her hard.

385
00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:22.090
To think that someone
actually showed up for her.

386
00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:26.850
Friends.

387
00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:30.190
That word... means pain.

388
00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:33.900
It breaks her heart.

389
00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:36.190
Usopp!

390
00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.440
Did Nami do all this to you?!

391
00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:40.570
Sorry. Zoro and I did that.

392
00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.320
No, you did!

393
00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:45.050
Luffy. You're here now.

394
00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:46.450
Yep. Sure am.

395
00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:48.540
I'm here, too. Hi there.

396
00:21:48.590 --> 00:21:50.580
One of these days I'll kill you.

397
00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:52.960
Oh! You just made a full recovery!

398
00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:53.670
Shut up!

399
00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:57.050
Oh, and by the way, we kinda heard
you were dead. Killed by Nami.

400
00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:59.210
– Huh?
– Stupid Johnny!

401
00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:01.420
He was spouting nonsense
that entire time!

402
00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:06.010
Well, in a way... it is the truth.

403
00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:10.430
But, I'm alive... 'cause you see,
she actually saved my life.

404
00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:12.670
Looks to me like she's got
some sorta hidden motive

405
00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:15.190
for hangin' out with
a bunch of renegade fishmen.

406
00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:17.510
– Obviously.
– Fine. What next?

407
00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:19.320
We gonna destroy Arlong Park?

408
00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:20.860
Whoa! Hang on just a second!

409
00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:23.520
Don't you think we'd better find
out what's going on with Nami first?

410
00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:25.660
It's no use either way.

411
00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:29.580
No matter what you guys do,
Arlong's rule won't come to an end.

412
00:22:29.730 --> 00:22:30.830
Nojiko.

413
00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:31.860
Who's she?

414
00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:32.830
Nami's big sister.

415
00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:36.470
What?! Nami's sister.
No wonder she's so hot!

416
00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:38.460
What do you mean that "it's no use"?

417
00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:40.800
Just trust me. Don't
get yourselves involved

418
00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:44.170
in what's going on here.
And leave poor Nami alone.

419
00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:45.510
I'll explain the situation.

420
00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:49.010
Yeah. And if that doesn't get
you to leave, I don't know what will.

421
00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:51.730
Look, there's
a Marine ship at the shore!

422
00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:53.710
It's branch 16's ship!

423
00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:58.320
Maybe headquarters is finally taking action
after what happened to branch 77!

424
00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:04.950
I'm Colonel Nezumi of branch 16.

425
00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:08.810
Now then. Genzo, please step up.
And make it snappy.

426
00:23:08.810 --> 00:23:11.680
Yes, Colonel.
I'm the one you're looking for.

427
00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:15.750
You, huh?
Take me to Nami's house at once!

428
00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:17.500
Nami? But why?

429
00:23:17.650 --> 00:23:19.840
I don't understand
what's going on, Colonel.

430
00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:23.260
Lead the way. That is
all you'll need to do.

